xnulinux is made of parts under different licenses, kept apart along the line between the Linux kernel and XNU.
Each source file names its license in an SPDX-License-Identifier line; the full texts are in LICENSES/:

  GPL-2.0-only         fki-ko/, linux/, scripts/, tools/, tests/, docs/, gpu/xnu-drm/xnudrmd.c, gpu/venus/
  GPL-2.0-or-later     gpu/xnu-cpu-metal/
  APSL-2.0             xnu-ko/, xnu-patches/, kexts/ (kexts/free/compat/ too)
  BSD-2-Clause-Patent  kexts/XnuDisplay/, kexts/XnuEthernet/, kexts/XnuInput/ (from macOS-DroidVM),
                       gpu/xnu-cpu-metal/src/xnu-cpu-metal-bundle/XnuCpuMetalShim.h (from UniXNU/AdrenoMetal)
  MPL-2.0              kexts/free/patches/corecrypto-arm64e-sptr.patch (a patch to corecrypto, under its license)
  MIT                  gpu/xnu-drm/darwin/, gpu/xnu-drm/xnudrm_proto.h; the patches to Mesa and virglrenderer
                       (under their upstream's license, as are the patches to metal2vulkan: GPL-2.0-or-later)

docs/images/ holds screenshots of macOS running on xnulinux; the macOS interface and wallpaper in them are Apple's.

Files without a comment syntax (JSON manifests, property lists, patches) are under the license of the directory they are in.

